From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 22:13:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01868/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE A2 (THE
 HEADLINE GATE, gated_on A1 selector_trained) -- does the ORACLE-DISTINCT
 learned ARC verifier BEAT majority vote OFF-ORACLE? On a HELD-OUT ARC split
 (disjoint from A1 folds), rerank with the A1 learned verifier
 (verifier_is_oracle=false; does NOT execute demos) vs majority-vote vs a
 MATCHED no-verifier control (same candidates/budget) vs oracle@K (the
 positive-control ceiling) vs an ARBITER conservative-override arm (keep vote
 unless the learned margin clears a fixed threshold, arXiv:2605.26172 / AggLM
 2509.06870). The LOAD-BEARING gate: verifier@1 - vote@1, bootstrap CI95
 EXCLUDES 0 AND headroom exists. YES -> the first oracle-distinct verifier win
 (closes GAP-3-ties-vote; informs the DiffusionGemma gate). TIE-with-headroom
 -> honest null. No-headroom -> uninformative (FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK, not a
 verifier failure).

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
